  );
}
All inputs are plain strings – no HTML is being stored. The preview is rendered on the client side using the same Mustache template as the server; because we never render user‑provided HTML directly, XSS is impossible. When a user finally clicks Download PDF, the server merges the JSON data into the Mustache template, applies the selected colour variables, and runs Puppeteer to create a PDF.

6️⃣ Security Hardening Checklist
Threat	Countermeasure (implemented in the code)
Man‑in‑the‑middle (MITM)	TLS termination at Nginx (letsencrypt) + HSTS header (Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload)
Brute‑Force login	express-rate-limit (5 attempts per 10 min per IP) + account lockout after 5 failed attempts (30 min)
SQL Injection	All DB calls use parameterised queries ($1, $2…) via pg. No raw string concatenation.
Cross‑Site Scripting (XSS)	- No user‑generated HTML is stored.
- Server‑side rendering uses Mustache (HTML escaped by default).
- Client‑side uses sanitize-html on the JSON payload before saving.
- CSP blocks inline scripts (except those whitelisted for reCAPTCHA).
CSRF	JWT stored in HttpOnly SameSite‑Strict cookies. All state‑changing endpoints also verify the JWT server‑side.
Cookie theft	HttpOnly + Secure flags, SameSite=Strict, short‑lived access token (15 min) + rotating refresh token.
Password compromise	Bcrypt (cost 12), unique salts for each password.
Malicious file upload	Avatar upload handled by Multer: mime‑type check (image/*), size limit 2 MiB, file renamed with UUID, stored outside the web‑root (or S3 with private ACL).
DoS / Resource Exhaustion	Global rate‑limit, per‑endpoint limit on file size, Puppeteer runs in a dedicated container with a max‑memory flag.
Information leakage	Error messages deliberately generic (e.g., “Invalid credentials”). Detailed stack traces are logged server‑side only.
Logging & alerting	Every login / signup attempt stored in login_logs / signup_logs. Admin endpoint /api/admin/login-logs returns the latest 100 rows. You can hook a daily cron to email you on spikes.
ReCAPTCHA	(Optional but recommended) add Google reCAPTCHA v3 token to /login and /signup payload; verify server‑side via Google API.
7️⃣ 50+ CV Templates – How to Add More
Create a template directory templates/ in the repo.

For each new design:

